A||N||3||862M4inCA||Timing gear problems.||||8||
Z||000000||862M4inCA||11-09-2000||11:58 AM||||Well guys, as some of you may recall early last month, I was planning on driving my car from CA to TX. Well it made it, sort of, I was ALMOST into Austin when my engine died suddenly. After a quick check of things it appeared that I busted a timing gear. Currently I have no where I can work on the thing to fix it (I'm living in an apartment where they really look for things like that) and was wondering if anyone has any idea where I could take it to either do it myself, or have someone else do it around here. Also and ideas on if it's possible to do it without pulling the motor out. I've been told it's possible, but need more info, I'm sure it's not as simple as removing the timing cover, grabing the gear and pulling it out. hehe tho I wish! Any help is greatly appreciated. ||||reg||8
Z||000001||StuGood||11-09-2000||12:37 PM||||1986 2M4...  I assume the distributor rotor doesn't rotate when you crank the engine.  Is that what makes you believe the cam isn't turning?<P>Might ask your co-workers at Dell (or wherever it is) if they'd let you work on it at their place.  Can't hurt to ask - face it, Fieros are cool, and most of the Texans I met down in Austin are real friendly. ||||reg||5
Z||000002||MrPBody||11-09-2000||07:27 PM||||I hear that it can be done, but it's not easy.  Here's one account:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/l4-timinggear.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/l4-timinggear.htm</A> <P>Good luck!  I may someday need to do the same.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||862M4inCA||11-10-2000||01:31 AM||||Well Stu, what actually tripped me off to believe I busted a timing gear was that the rocker arms were stationary when I had someone crank over the motor while I looked in through the oil fill hole. From what I KNOW, that shouldn't happen unless a timing chain/belt, or in my case, gear has broken. Still on the lookout for places to do the work, but only being in town for a week now, and working at a grocery store (tho I WISH I was with Dell. hehe) my options have been pretty limited. <P>MrP: Thanx for the link...I'm going to check it out and then find a place to be able to do that.||||reg||1
